            {
              "id": "glog-0df4d402-e87d-4474-ad87-bae8ada11ca8",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Detected Issue with C Function: `memcpy`\n\nThe `memcpy` function in C/C++ is used to copy a specified number of bytes from a source memory location to a destination memory location. The vulnerability arises when the size of the data being copied (`sz`) exceeds the size of the destination buffer (`match`). This can lead to buffer overflow, which may result in undefined behavior, including data corruption, crashes, or security vulnerabilities such as arbitrary code execution.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Bounds Checking**: Always ensure that the destination buffer is large enough to hold the data being copied. Use safer alternatives like `memmove` or `strncpy` if applicable, which provide additional safety checks.\n2. **Use Safer Libraries**: Consider using safer libraries or functions that automatically handle buffer sizes, such as `std::copy` in C++.\n3. **Static Analysis Tools**: Utilize static analysis tools to detect potential buffer overflows during development.\n4. **Code Reviews**: Regularly perform code reviews to catch potential vulnerabilities early in the development process.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the specific vulnerability in the code snippet `memcpy(match, c, sz)`, ensure that the size of `match` is checked before performing the copy operation:\n\n```cpp\n#include <cstring> // Required for memcpy\n#include <algorithm> // Required for std::min\n\nvoid safe_memcpy(char* match, const char* c, size_t sz, size_t match_size) {\n    // Ensure that we do not copy more than the size of the destination buffer\n    size_t copy_size = std::min(sz, match_size);\n    memcpy(match, c, copy_size);\n}\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nTo execute the code example properly, the following library dependencies are required:\n\n- `<cstring>`: For the `memcpy` function.\n- `<algorithm>`: For the `std::min` function.\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-120](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)"
